{"c":[{"id":"a16996d817dbf8d7","sum":"semantic/embed heal torch once from a hashed freeze, else name sr-initialize; nightly: ensure-env; ingest && embed. Issue 147 chain is short-lived (~5-6 installs), own module, data-safe. DuckDB 2.0 (LTS to Oct 2027): new files v2.0.0+, unreadable before 2.0.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2344b5030265f7ee","sum":"semantic/embed restore torch once from a usable hashed freeze and retry; else say re-run sr-initialize. doctor smoke is report-only. Nightly payload: (date; stockroom shim ensure-env; stockroom ingest && stockroom embed): a failed heal still ingests; failed ingest skips embed.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261020T193116Z-270eb1650c4e7f96","text":"semantic and embed restore torch once from a usable hashed freeze and retry; no freeze, a failed restore, or any other encoder failure says re-run sr-initialize. doctor smoke stays report-only and still names ensure-env when a freeze exists.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261020T205704Z-a2498a1e20047fe3","text":"Nightly cron and launchd payload is (date; stockroom shim ensure-env; stockroom ingest && stockroom embed). A failed heal still ingests; a failed ingest still skips embed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1046806e8c5186a7","sum":"Issue 147 migration chain (copy, check, swap) is short-lived (~5-6 installs, a month or two), own module, reliable not bulletproof; data-safety holds. DuckDB 2.0.0 (LTS to Oct 2027; 1.5 to Mar 2027): suite passes; new files are v2.0.0+, unreadable before 2.0.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T145418Z-a7061b3a1a0c5bbf","text":"Issue 147 storage migration chain (verified copy, session-start check, swap) is short-lived: about 5-6 installs, kept a month or two, then removed. Build it reliable, not bulletproof; data-safety rules still hold. Keep it in its own module.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T155046Z-35a2088124b6c3aa","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 (2026-10-21, LTS to Oct 2027; 1.5 to Mar 2027): engine suite passes unchanged (uv --with overlay), vss loads, HNSW still used (EXPLAIN prints 'Hnsw Index Scan', not HNSW_INDEX_SCAN). New files are v2.0.0+ by default; DuckDB before 2.0 cannot read them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3969d97bee49fe6a","sum":"Releases stand alone; v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8 (tests make v1.0.0 on purpose). 1.5.4 replays a v1.0.0+ file a killed 2.0.0 writer left, and cannot open v2.0.0+. 2.0.0 zstd clause: BinderException on v1.0.0, ZSTD at v1.2.0+.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1f960dec0850b21e","sum":"Releases stand alone (users skip them); v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8; old-format tests create v1.0.0 on purpose. 1.5.4 opens and replays a v1.0.0+ file a killed 2.0.0 writer left; only v2.0.0+ files are unreadable.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T160004Z-0474312fdfee4cb0","text":"Every stockroom release must stand alone: users skip releases. Releases v0.1.0-v2.1.2 all pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so warehouses in the wild are v1.0.0+ at schema 1-8. Under DuckDB 2.0, tests that need an old-format file must create it at storage v1.0.0 on purpose.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T161737Z-639a1a68a7083e6a","text":"Measured 2026-10-21: DuckDB 1.5.4 opens (ro and rw) a v1.0.0+ file a crashed DuckDB 2.0.0 writer left with a wal, plain or vss HNSW-indexed, and replays all rows; the wal matches a 1.5.4 writer's in size. Only files 2.0 creates (v2.0.0+) are unreadable before 2.0.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c27c79ce59ec8d2","sum":"DuckDB 2.0.0: USING COMPRESSION zstd raises BinderException on v1.0.0 storage (1.5.4 ignores it); v1.2.0+ gives ZSTD, so zstd in 0001 breaks v1.0.0 fixtures. 2.0.0 wal replay into an HNSW index breaks it (InternalException or hang); DROP+CREATE+CHECKPOINT repairs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T164029Z-dd6c62dffb711e78","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 raises BinderException for USING COMPRESSION zstd at storage v1.0.0 (1.5.4 stored it uncompressed silently); v1.2.0+ storage gives ZSTD. A zstd clause in 0001 breaks a schema-0 v1.0.0+ file and old-format test fixtures built from current 0001.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T170926Z-f865c4bcdda86174","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 bug: replaying a wal holding inserts into an HNSW-indexed table (killed 1.5.4 or 2.0 writer) breaks the index: query, delete, insert raise InternalException (flat or constant vector) or hang. 1.5.4 replays fine. DROP INDEX, CREATE INDEX, CHECKPOINT repairs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
